 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "Thanos & Obosh",
 "notes": [
  "Companion: Obosh, the Preypiercer (outside the 100). Every nonland card must have an odd mana value or Obosh is illegal. No even-cost cards, ever (Coalition Victory was ruled out for this; he chose Obosh).",
  "Plan: cast Thanos ({R}{W}{B}), then power-up for {C}{W}{U}{B}{R}{G} (only {C}{U}{G} the turn he enters). Always choose EVEN: his creatures are all odd, so the wipe is one-sided. Obosh doubles damage from odd sources: Thanos, Jeska, Mayhem Devil, Bastion.",
  "The {C} is true colorless, and it's the bottleneck. Colorless sources: Sol Ring, Worn Powerstone, Basalt Monolith, Plaza of Heroes, Rogue's Passage, Villainous Hideout, Secluded Courtyard (name Villain), Unknown Shores.",
  "Plaza of Heroes and Villainous Hideout can pay any symbol of the power-up once Thanos is out. Oscorp Industries taps for U, B or R only.",
  "Repeat wipes: Ephemerate, Conjurer's Closet or Venser's +2 blinks Thanos, so he 'entered this turn' and the power-up costs just {C}{U}{G} again.",
  "Tokens are mana value 0 (even), so his own tokens die to the wipe too. Bastion of Remembrance turns that into drain. Mister Sinister's Thrulls reset this way before he hits seven.",
  "Game Changers (3): Opposition Agent, Mystical Tutor, Aura Shards. Mystic Remora: draw off it 2–3 turns, then let it go.",
  "Changes since Oct 17 rebuild: Champion's Helm → Ephemerate; Forest, Island → Secluded Courtyard, Unknown Shores; Rhystic Study → Mystic Remora; Teferi's Protection → Mystical Tutor; Painful Truths → Narset → Aura Shards.",
  "Odd-cost upgrade ideas if a villain is a dud: Esper Sentinel, Skullclamp, Vindicate, Generous Gift, Swan Song, Gilded Lotus, Palladium Myr. Avoid Ancient Tomb/Mana Vault (Game Changers) and Mind Stone/Thran Dynamo (even).",
  "Not all Marvel card mana values were confirmed. Moxfield will flag an illegal Obosh on import if one is even.",
  "Nov 4, 2026: cut Aang's Shelter. It's Teferi's Protection under another name, and that made a 4th Game Changer. Venser, the Sojourner took the open slot, so the deck is back to 100."
 ],
